<title>UK: Lancaster to succeed Smith in Hepworth chair.</title>
<headline>Lancaster to succeed Smith in Hepworth chair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK bulding and home products group Hepworth Plc said on Thursday its chairman Sir Roland Smith will retire from the board at its annual general meeting in May.</p>
<p>Smith will be succeeded by Jeremy Lancaster who joins the board now as non-executive deputy chairman.</p>
<p>Lancaster is also chairman of Rexam Plc and was formerly chairman and chief executive of Wolseley Plc. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
